20. What I would change immediately

For your current project, these are the must-fix issues:

Issue	Priority
Remove Users.tasksId	🔴 Critical
Add Task → User assignTo relation	🔴 Critical
Add Task → User assignBy relation	🔴 Critical
Add Project → User createdBy relation	🔴 Critical
Add Project → User updatedBy relation	🔴 Critical
Add User ↔ Project many-to-many	🔴 Critical
Remove Tasks.name @unique	🟠 Important
Add indexes to FK fields	🟠 Important
Add defaults for role/status	🟠 Important
Replace timeline with startDate/endDate	🟠 Important
Consider nullable phone	🟡 Depends
Add comments	🟡 Future
Add attachments	🟡 Future
Add activity/audit log	🟡 Future
Add workspace/organization	🟡 Production SaaS
Add soft delete	🟡 Production
Add task position	🟡 Future
The most important relationship design

I'd make your MVP database:

User
 ├── createdProjects
 ├── updatedProjects
 ├── projectMemberships
 ├── assignedTasks
 └── assignedByTasks

Project
 ├── createdByUser
 ├── updatedByUser
 ├── members
 └── tasks

Task
 ├── project
 ├── assignee
 └── assigner

That gives you a clean foundation for:

User → Projects → Tasks → Assigned Users

and avoids the biggest relational problems in your current schema.

One other thing: because you're using the newer Prisma setup where your datasource db currently has no url, I would keep that part as-is if you've already moved the connection configuration into prisma.config.ts; don't re-add url to schema.prisma just to fix these relation issues.